{"name":"Garden Snail","hex":"#cdb1ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garden snail","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Cornu aspersum, a species of helicid snails commonly found in gardens; originally native to the Mediterranean region, now spread throughout Europe and introduced to the British Isles, the Americas, Australia and New Zealand, among other locations."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden_snail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cornu aspersum","blocks":[{"text":"Cornu aspersum, known by the common name garden snail, is a species of land snail in the family Helicidae, which includes some of the most familiar land snails. Of all terrestrial molluscs, this species may be the most widely known. It was classified under the name Helix aspersa for over two centuries, but the prevailing classification now places it in the genus Cornu."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Snail1web.jpg/330px-Snail1web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornu_aspersum","wikidata":"Q22019793"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","wikidata":"Q1107656"},{"title":"Snail","blocks":[{"text":"A snail is a shelled gastropod. The name is most often applied to land snails, terrestrial pulmonate gastropod molluscs. However, the common name snail is also used for most of the members of the molluscan class Gastropoda that have a coiled shell that is large enough for the animal to retract completely into. When the word \"snail\" is used in this most general sense, it includes not just land snails but also numerous species of sea snails and freshwater snails. Gastropods that naturally lack a shell, or have only an internal shell, are mostly called slugs, and land snails that have only a very small shell are sometimes called semi-slugs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Snail.jpg/330px-Snail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snail","wikidata":"Q308841"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Cornu_aspersum_Presence_in_European_countries.png/500px-Cornu_aspersum_Presence_in_European_countries.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Cornu_aspersum_Presence_in_European_countries.png/500px-Cornu_aspersum_Presence_in_European_countries.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACornu_aspersum_Presence_in_European_countries.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Snail-wiki-120-Zachi-Evenor.jpg/500px-Snail-wiki-120-Zachi-Evenor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Snail-wiki-120-Zachi-Evenor.jpg/1280px-Snail-wiki-120-Zachi-Evenor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Snail-wiki-120-Zachi-Evenor.jpg/500px-Snail-wiki-120-Zachi-Evenor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cornu aspersum in warm regions commonly emerges in moist weather in winter.","link